# Weatherman Mockup Creator Rules

## Tech Stack & Architecture
- **Language:** Python 3.10+
- **Core Libraries:** Pillow (PIL), OpenCV, ReportLab, Streamlit, PyMuPDF.
- **Design Specs:** Strict adherence to Weatherman production worksheet standards (e.g., Walk/Golf Essential panels, standard 21.6cm x 10cm artwork bounds; Venture Dry Pack and Trek Hat Paula 1:1 page maps).

## Guardrails & Execution
- Always maintain exact coordinate mappings, aspect ratios, and scaling factors when projecting client logos onto umbrella panels.
- Keep UI code cleanly decoupled from the image-processing and PDF-export modules inside `utils/`.
- Ensure generated multi-view proofs mirror official production sheets (Front View, Top View, Sleeve, Flat Pattern, and Hat Side/Front layouts).
- Keep `BACKPACK_STATIC_PAGE_MAP` and `HAT_STATIC_PAGE_MAP` intact — serve Paula PDF pages 1:1; do not recalculate Front View / tech-pack coordinates on those paths.
- Keep Backpack, Hat, Poncho, and Umbrella pipelines isolated (family-scoped fabrics, logo colors, and exporters).
- Reference sheets: @Proper Brands x WM Umbrella 2026 Mockup Designs.pdf @Proper Brands x WM Umbrella 2026 Mockup Designs v2.pdf @Hats-Mockups.pdf
